---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Building Tools, Not Just Papers: Why I Code" description="Why building systems alongside papers is essential">
  <div class="container-content py-16">
    <article class="max-w-2xl">
      <a href="/blog/" class="link-arrow mb-6 inline-flex">
        ← All posts
      </a>
      <p class="font-mono text-[0.65rem] text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-3">Essay · 2026-06-15</p>
      <h1 class="mb-8">Building Tools, Not Just Papers: Why I Code</h1>
      <div class="prose-page text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text)] space-y-4">
        <p>When I started this research, I chose to develop both manuscripts and inspectable research systems for studying miscalibrated advice.</p>
        <p>CheckMyCoach is more than a manuscript concept: it includes 44 passing tests, a functioning API pipeline, a Streamlit frontend, and an observed API cost of approximately $0.001 per attempted correction in the evaluated configuration.</p>
        <p>Why does this matter? Because <strong>trust calibration research benefits from inspectable implementations.</strong> Implemented prototypes make assumptions, failure modes, and future human-study designs concrete.</p>
        <p>For released artifacts, I provide quick-start instructions, environment information, tests, and versioned schemas where available.</p>
        <p>Reproducibility status is reported separately for each project; independent reproduction and cross-lab convergence are not assumed from documentation alone.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
